An intense and highly concentrated beam of light.

717
00:53:00,280 --> 00:53:03,940
And for some uses, quite possibly, the ultimate non-lethal weapon.

718
00:53:03,941 --> 00:53:11,820
While lasers have existed since the 1960s, only in recent years has the technology matured

719
00:53:11,821 --> 00:53:16,580
to the point of practical use.

720
00:53:16,581 --> 00:53:21,020
And military non-lethal weapons developers want to harness that technology for use in

721
00:53:21,021 --> 00:53:24,440
something called mission kill.

722
00:53:24,441 --> 00:53:30,780
It's a term strategists use to describe disabling an enemy's control systems in weapons machinery.

723
00:53:30,781 --> 00:53:36,680
If you render the enemy's machinery inoperable, you kill his mission without necessarily having to kill him.

724
00:53:37,760 --> 00:53:42,760
In some cases, you just want to immobilize a unit or you want to immobilize their equipment

725
00:53:42,761 --> 00:53:46,220
or just prevent it from working as effectively for a limited period of time.

726
00:53:46,400 --> 00:53:48,580
The goal is not always to destroy something.

727
00:53:49,760 --> 00:53:53,280
The laser, many feel, might be the perfect instrument for this approach.

728
00:53:54,680 --> 00:54:00,580
A laser, one actually capable of destruction, would allow for a very precise application of force.

729
00:54:00,780 --> 00:54:09,720
For example, if you found a rocket launcher, and with a laser, potentially, if you could just shoot the wings off of it so it can't fly,

